  "result": "Perfect! All 263 tests pass (31 new statement tests added). Customer statement functionality is now complete:\n\n**src/statements.js (new file):**\n- `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` generates a customer payment statement\n  - Returns ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })\n  - Filters invoices by:\n    - Customer ID (normalized)\n    - Status: 'issued' or 'partially_paid' only\n    - Issue date on or before asOf date\n  - Each invoice includes:\n    - number: invoice number\n    - issueDate: date invoice was created\n    - dueDate: payment due date\n    - total: full invoice amount (calculated via invoiceTotals)\n    - due: amount still owed (calculated via balanceDue)\n  - Invoices sorted by issueDate (ascending)\n  - totalDue: sum of all due amounts\n  - Returns CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND for unknown customer\n\n**test/statements.test.js (31 comprehensive tests):**\n- Basic structure and return values\n- Unknown customer rejection\n- Status filtering (includes issued/partially_paid, excludes draft/paid)\n- Date filtering (on/before asOf, excludes future invoices)\n- Customer filtering with normalization\n- Invoice data completeness\n- Due amount calculations (full for unpaid, balance for partial)\n- Total due summation (multiple invoices, mixed payment states)\n- Sorting by issue date\n- Edge cases: empty lists, large invoice counts, mixed statuses\n- Date comparison across years\n\nThe statement function integrates seamlessly with existing payment tracking to show customers their outstanding balance by invoice.",
